WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:07.688
Politicians love pointing to one giant number: GDP—now over a hundred trillion dollars globally! Wait, what does it actually measure?

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:14.902
GDP means Gross Domestic Product: the total price tag of every brand-new good or service sold, from lattes to rocket launches!

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:21.905
Here is the catch: we only count the final receipt—never raw ingredients twice—and only things made inside a country's borders.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:30.243
The secret formula is C + I + G + Net Exports! C is consumer spending—nearly 70% of America's economy.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:37.998
I is business investment in robots and factories. G is government building bridges and schools, plus exports minus imports!

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:44.825
Wait—what if prices just inflated? That is why economists use Real GDP, stripping out inflation to reveal true growth.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:52.550
Plot twist! Simon Kuznets invented GDP in 1934, warning Congress it is not well-being. It ignores clean air and parenting!

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:59.845
GDP is an economic speedometer: it shows how fast our engine spins, just not if we are driving somewhere worth going—and that is huge!
